<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android Auto Backup rules (API 23+).

  Net effect: nothing leaves the device. That is deliberate, not an oversight.

  An <include> list restricts backup to exactly what it names, and the one domain named here
  is empty in practice: FlowReader has no SharedPreferences at all (there is no
  getSharedPreferences / PreferenceManager call in the app). Settings live in DataStore
  Preferences, and `dataStoreFile()` resolves to filesDir/datastore/settings.preferences_pb,
  which belongs to the `file` domain — not `sharedpref`. The Room database, the FTS database,
  covers and reader background images are all in `file` / `database` too, so they are excluded
  by the same restriction.

  Do NOT "fix" this by adding <include domain="file" .../>. Backing up the preferences file
  would ship a user's reading habits off-device through Google's backup transport, which
  contradicts the offline-first, no-network-sync design. Users who want their data on another
  device use the in-app backup/export (SAF file or LAN transfer), which they trigger explicitly.

  Security note: no credentials are stored anywhere today. If a future version ever adds an
  account or sync feature, keep its secrets in EncryptedSharedPreferences and out of backup.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <!-- Restricts backup to `sharedpref`, which this app never writes to. -->
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="."/>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="device.xml"/>
</full-backup-content>
